1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:01,307
One joke on late-night TV

2
00:00:01,307 --> 00:00:03,595
emptied store shelves across America...

3
00:00:03,595 --> 00:00:05,469
for a shortage that didn't exist.

4
00:00:05,469 --> 00:00:07,884
December 1973.

5
00:00:07,884 --> 00:00:10,856
Gas lines. Oil crisis.

6
00:00:10,856 --> 00:00:12,413
Everyone's already on edge.

7
00:00:12,413 --> 00:00:14,317
A congressman warns the U.S. MAY

8
00:00:14,317 --> 00:00:16,465
face a toilet paper shortage...

9
00:00:16,465 --> 00:00:17,494
in a few months.

10
00:00:17,494 --> 00:00:19,881
The Tonight Show drops the "may."

11
00:00:19,881 --> 00:00:22,424
Johnny Carson tells about 20 million viewers:

12
00:00:22,424 --> 00:00:24,246
there's a toilet paper shortage.

13
00:00:24,246 --> 00:00:24,919
Within days,

14
00:00:24,919 --> 00:00:26,640
carts are FULL of rolls.

15
00:00:26,640 --> 00:00:28,590
Stores set limits.

16
00:00:28,590 --> 00:00:30,309
One raises the price from 39¢

17
00:00:30,309 --> 00:00:32,596
to 69¢ a roll.

18
00:00:32,596 --> 00:00:33,928
Shelves are still empty.

19
00:00:33,928 --> 00:00:36,099
But here's the thing...

20
00:00:36,099 --> 00:00:38,083
nobody was being dumb.

21
00:00:38,083 --> 00:00:39,917
If you hear about a shortage,

22
00:00:39,917 --> 00:00:41,938
and the shelf is empty...

23
00:00:41,938 --> 00:00:43,818
buying extra is the SMART move.

24
00:00:43,818 --> 00:00:45,014
Everyone made the smart move.

25
00:00:45,014 --> 00:00:46,998
And THAT was the shortage.

26
00:00:46,998 --> 00:00:48,960
The factories never stopped.

27
00:00:48,960 --> 00:00:50,829
Carson later told viewers:

28
00:00:50,829 --> 00:00:52,322
there is no shortage.

29
00:00:52,322 --> 00:00:55,352
A shortage doesn't need missing toilet paper.

30
00:00:55,352 --> 00:00:57,767
It just needs everyone to believe in it...

31
00:00:57,767 --> 00:00:59,960
at the same time.
